  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The current best result (config_032: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat; acc=0.688) shows a modest +0.035 gain over the best rna_only multiprofile config (0.653), and image-only resnet50 was very weak (0.208). The key uncertainty is whether the image modality's limited contribution is due to the weak resnet50 encoder or is a fundamental limitation of the image modality for this task. config_038 is identical to config_032 except it swaps resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l, providing a clean single-variable A/B comparison that isolates image encoder quality. If ViT-L substantially improves multimodal performance, it validates investing in the image modality and opens the ViT-L multimodal space; if it does not, it indicates the image modality is inherently limited here and future budget should focus on RNA-side improvements. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves a major design axis (image encoder quality) that has zero prior evidence, and the answer will shape all subsequent multimodal decisions."
}

